{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR REQUIREMENT + PRE-IMPLEMENTATION VERIFICATION: per-pass model parity on cutover.\n\nREQUIREMENT (operator, this run): after the Bedrock cutover the code-review agent must use COMPARABLE models per pass — Pass-1 on opus for many/all of its criteria, Pass-2 (verify) and Pass-4 (coach) on sonnet.\n\nVERIFIED AGAINST LANDED CODE (worktree feat/llm-provider-seam @ 8465873ec). As written this story CANNOT satisfy that requirement, for three INDEPENDENT reasons:\n\n(1) Code review has NO per-pass model split today, on ANY provider. src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/code-review.yaml (190 lines) declares no `model:` and no `model_ladder:` on any step, so base/round_a/round_b (Pass-1), verify (Pass-2, `temperature: 0` at :155) and coach (Pass-4) ALL resolve to cfg.model via resolve_model (step > workflow > config). The sonnet downgrade this requirement assumes exists ONLY in plan-review: _verifier_cfg (plan_review/__init__.py:46-70) -> review_kernel.resolve_verifier_model. Consumers of resolve_verifier_model are plan_review/{__init__,xcheck,orchestrator,workflow_ops}.py and completion.py — code_review calls it NOWHERE. So the code-review agent currently runs Pass-1, Pass-2 AND Pass-4 all on claude-opus-4-8. Satisfying the requirement is therefore NEW WORK, not preservation of existing behaviour — worth stating plainly because \"use comparable models\" reads like a no-op parity ask and is not one.\n\n(2) The one downgrade rule that DOES exist inverts on Bedrock. review_kernel/verify.py:269 is `verifier_default if model == default_model else (model or verifier_default)`, with default_model = \"claude-opus-4-8\". ANY Bedrock id (\"bedrock:us.anthropic....\") is a non-default value, read as an explicit operator choice, and returned unchanged. Consequence: on cutover plan-review's Pass-2/Pass-4 STOP downgrading and follow Pass-1 onto whichever single Bedrock model REBAR_LLM_MODEL names. This story's Scope is exactly that one env var (\"infra/compose/ — the bot service's REBAR_LLM_MODEL\"), i.e. ONE knob for FOUR passes.\n\n(3) Bare `claude-*` names route to ANTHROPIC, not Bedrock. config.py:333-341 _PROVIDER_PREFIXES maps prefix \"claude\" -> \"anthropic\". plan-review.yaml:62-65 sets Pass-1's model_ladder to bare [claude-haiku-4-5, claude-sonnet-4-6, claude-opus-4-8]. After a cutover that only re-points REBAR_LLM_MODEL, that ladder STILL resolves to direct Anthropic — a SPLIT-BRAIN where the Pass-1 finder keeps calling Anthropic while everything else is on Bedrock. Bedrock needs inference-profile ids (us.anthropic....) which match no prefix rule, so every ladder/step model must be rewritten provider-aware, not merely re-pointed.\n\nNOT A USABLE SECOND KNOB: cfg.bedrock_model_id / REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID is parsed from env (config.py:521, 633-638) and documented in docs/env-vars.md:55 but is READ BY NOTHING — no consumer in src/ or tests/. It is dead config as landed by S3 and cannot carry a per-pass mapping until it is wired up. (Filing that as its own defect.)\n\nWHY THIS IS URGENT, NOT COST-COSMETIC — measured this run, in the project account 896586841071/us-east-1:\n- Pass-2 pins temperature=0 (code-review.yaml:155). us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 + temperature=0 -> ModelHTTPError 400 \"temperature is deprecated for this model\". Resolving Pass-2 onto an opus profile can HARD-FAIL the gate, not just overspend. S3's supports_temperature override (capabilities.py:95) lists opus-4-7 ONLY.\n- us. AND global. opus-4-5 report cache_read=0 / cache_write=0 while billing full input; us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 caches. An opus-everywhere cutover also loses caching SILENTLY.\n- Conversely a sonnet-everywhere cutover (DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID = us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6) silently DOWNGRADES Pass-1 from opus — a finder-quality regression no existing test would catch.\nSo both single-model cutovers are wrong, in opposite directions. This is exactly the gap the operator flagged.\n\nPROPOSED AC ADDITIONS (this story, or a new sibling if the config seam turns out large):\n- [ ] the cutover configures the Pass-1 and Pass-2/Pass-4 model ids INDEPENDENTLY\n- [ ] a test asserts the RESOLVED model for each pass under a Bedrock config is the intended class (opus-family for Pass-1; sonnet-family for Pass-2/Pass-4)\n- [ ] no bare `claude-*` model id survives on any path the bot executes post-cutover (else it silently routes to Anthropic)\n- [ ] [operator-attested] a real post-cutover vote's sidecar shows the per-pass model ids actually used, citing the change id\n\nNOT fixed inside this story's current Scope because the requirement needs a config seam that does not exist (one env var cannot express four passes), and that seam is a design decision rather than an implementation detail — same class as 2682 (runner.py at the cap) and the providers.py 299/300 blocker on 343b. Raising it in the PLAN rather than leaving an implementer facing an unwinnable constraint."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785435445343336001,"uuid":"c22d1085-526a-4833-93e6-b501ef760231"}